#!/usr/bin/env vml
# ============================================================================
#   Bob: builds Visualised. Linux on this computer (tools/build-local.sh),
#   Windows on A8 over SSH (tools/build-windows.sh), one at a time or both at
#   once, with a light, the stage it's at and the time it's taken for each,
#   and every line of each build on its own tab.
#
#   Set up… says where the repo is (~/projects/vml-github unless you say)
#   and which Windows PC builds for Windows (a8, a name from ~/.ssh/config).
#   They're kept as the preferences bob_repo and bob_host; BOB_REPO and
#   BOB_HOST in the environment win over both.
#   Away from desk locks this computer and the Windows PC, and logs how long
#   you were away (~/.local/share/bob/away.csv: date, away, back, minutes),
#   with today's total along the foot.
#   Run it as a program: chmod +x Bob.vml, then ./Bob.vml
#   Each build's log is also kept in ~/.cache/bob-linux.log and
#   ~/.cache/bob-windows.log.
#
#   Made with Visualised.
# ============================================================================

